## Task 5 — unit 1 consultation (countsCore.ts, counts.test.ts, tsconfig.eval.json)

Question: full Unit 1 diff pasted (parseCountsBlock/parsePlan/parseReport/
parseSuiteLog/reconcile/verdict/formatResult in eval/bin/countsCore.ts, plus
the 14 unit tests), asked for a verdict on soundness to commit, concrete bugs,
and whether the `nothing`-outranks-`mismatch` precedence can be defeated —
given the CLI (Unit 2) was designed to layer a per-supplied-document "nothing"
check on top of `reconcile`'s own combined-claims check, rather than having
`reconcile` itself know about per-document emptiness.

Advisor's self-reported model, quoted verbatim: "I am **Claude Opus 5 (1M
context)**; exact model ID **`claude-opus-5[1m]`**."

Summary of the answer: sound to commit but fix two things first. (1) The
CLI-side split for per-document "nothing" was the real design flaw — it makes
`Result.status` a value the CLI can silently override, defeats the literal
`NOTHING TO CHECK: <document> yielded 0 claims (<why>)` message the plan
specifies, and weakens M1's intended end-to-end kill (test 23 would exit 2 via
the CLI's own check even if `verdict` were mutated to always return 'ok').
Fix: pass a `supplied` list into `reconcile` itself so it computes the
per-document emptiness and folds it into `status` before returning — `verdict`
and its verbatim `if (claims.length === 0) return 'nothing'` line are
untouched. (2) The `prose-lessons` MISMATCH message text itself matched
`PROSE_LESSONS` (`/\b(\d+) lessons\b/g`), so quoting a red retro run verbatim
into TASK5-REPORT.md in unit 3 would self-trigger new prose claims and break
the unit-3 self-run. Also flagged: the `generators` ok-line printed the full
224-id registry on every claim; an empty `generators:`/`lesson-ids:` value
parsed as a valid empty-list claim that trivially passes; `sectionOffset`
computed via `indexOf` rather than exact arithmetic (correct today, fragile);
a double "ERROR: … ERROR: …" prefix in `formatResult`'s error branch; the
mismatch count derived by re-scanning lines for the substring "MISMATCH"
rather than the counter already held in `reconcile`; and several mutation
blind spots in `buildProseLessonUniverse`, `normaliseCourse` and
`SUITE_GREEN`'s equality check that the 14-test suite doesn't yet exercise.
Confirmed the `nothing`-outranks-`mismatch` precedence in `verdict()` itself
is correct and cannot be defeated from inside `countsCore.ts` — the risk was
entirely that Unit 2 would become a second authority on it.

Action taken: all five concrete findings applied before commit (reconcile now
takes `supplied` and computes `empty`/folds it into `status`; prose-lessons
reason text reworded off the swept phrasing; generators actual value
summarised instead of dumping the registry; empty `generators`/`lesson-ids`
values now a parse error; `sectionOffset` computed by exact length arithmetic).
Also applied the double-ERROR-prefix fix and switched the mismatch count to
the counter tracked during reconciliation. Extra test assertions added for
the `normaliseCourse` absolute-prefix case, `SUITE_GREEN`'s unequal-pair case,
and the `buildProseLessonUniverse` per-level/total-only membership cases the
advisor flagged as under-tested. Gates re-run after the fixes before
committing (see the unit-1 commit message and its gate numbers).

## Task 5 — unit 2 consultation (countsTree.ts, counts.ts, counts.sh, fixtures, retro tests)

Question: full Unit 2 diff pasted (countsTree.ts's loadFacts, counts.ts's
CLI, counts.sh's wrapper, the three transcription fixtures, and 11 more
tests reconciling plans 1-4 against a generated tree snapshot plus three
end-to-end spawn tests of the real binary) — asked whether the CLI actually
preserves "nothing outranks mismatch, never silently exit 0" end to end,
whether countsTree's dynamic-import fact loading has correctness risk,
whether the hand-rolled argument parser has edge cases, whether the
`process.argv.slice(2)` fix (found in the unit-2 build: this container's
`process.argv` under `npx vite-node` is `[node, vite-node-bin,
...scriptArgs]`, contradicting TASK5-PLAN.md section 8 item 5's claimed
`[vite-node-bin, ...scriptArgs]`) is actually right or just lucky for this
container, and whether the three spawn tests exercise the real binary or
could pass vacuously.

Advisor's self-reported model, quoted verbatim: "**Opus 5 (1M context)** —
exact model ID `claude-opus-5[1m]`."

Summary of the answer: sound to commit after two must-fix bugs. Verified the
core precedence property directly against the real `counts.sh` binary across
all four supplied-document combinations, confirming `nothing` outranks
`mismatch` end to end. Found (B1, must-fix): `void main()` meant an
uncaught rejection inside `main` — e.g. a stray non-course file dropped into
`src/content/courses/` — became an unhandled-rejection exit of 1, which
`counts.sh`'s own documented contract assigns to "mismatch", making a broken
tool indistinguishable from disagreeing documents; reproduced live. Found
(B2, should-fix): `process.exit()` after a large `console.log` can truncate
piped stdout (measured ~64KB threshold under vite-node), which would silently
drop the verdict line on a long run through a pipe while the exit code
survives; fixed by using `process.exitCode` and returning rather than calling
`process.exit()` after output. Found (B3): confirmed my `slice(2)` finding
independently (byte-identical argv reproduction), but suggested deriving the
split from wherever the `vite-node` binary itself sits in argv rather than
hard-coding either index, since that is the one thing both observed layouts
agree on — implemented as `scriptArgs()` in countsCore.ts with a unit test
covering both layouts plus a no-match fallback. Found (B4, minor): a course
file exporting two course-shaped values would silently pick the first via
`.find()`; changed to `.filter()` + throw unless exactly one. Also flagged
(B5, non-blocking follow-up, not applied — out of the plan's stated file
scope which excludes package.json): `vite-node` isn't a pinned dependency of
this repo, fetched fresh via npx. Confirmed the three end-to-end spawn tests
are genuine (not vacuous) with one tightened assertion suggested
(`.not.toBe('ok')` → `.toBe('mismatch')`, since the claim being tested is
deterministic). Separately and pointedly: ran counts.sh against its own plan
with a real suite log and got `COUNTS DISAGREE` — TASK5-PLAN.md's own
`tests: 3111` block is now stale against the tree's actual 3116 (soon 3117),
and the plan's stated "25 tests" is now 31 — advised reporting this
divergence rather than editing the frozen plan to force a green run, since
that would be exactly the fabrication this task exists to prevent.

Action taken: B1 (main().catch(), proper ERROR + exit 2 on a harness fault
— verified live against a real stray-file crash before this fix showed a raw
stack trace at exit 1, after it shows a clean ERROR at exit 2), B2
(process.exitCode instead of process.exit after output, on both the
--dump-facts and the main result path), B3 (scriptArgs() in countsCore.ts,
plus a 3-case unit test), B4 (filter+throw-unless-exactly-one in
countsTree.ts), and the test tightening were all applied before commit. B5
is recorded as a follow-up, not applied (package.json is outside this task's
stated file scope). The plan's own tests: 3111 staleness is carried into the
